    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual</a></i> </p><p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Construction\" title=\"Lightsaber Construction\">Lightsaber Construction</a></i> </p><p>A Beckon Call is a small <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Communications_Devices\" title=\"Communications Devices\">Communications Device</a> that links up with the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Slave_Circuit\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Slave Circuit\">Slave Circuits</a> on a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Starship\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Starship\">Starship</a>. When activated, the Beckon Call transmits a signal to the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a> it is linked to, activating it's autopilot programming and summoning the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a> to the nearest safe spot close to the wielder. A Beckon Call functions only when connected to a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a> with a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Slave_Circuit\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Slave Circuit\">Slave Circuit</a>. </p>",
